  "body": "This is a change in response to w3c/manifest#1069 which changes the interface of the \"processing a manifest\" algorithm to take document and manifest URLs instead of a Link and Response element.\n\nThe change on this side exactly preserves the existing behaviour. Note that a few new steps are added: these steps were removed from the Manifest spec in w3c/manifest#1069 to make the interface more versatile. The steps have been added into HTML to preserve the existing behaviour and call the Manifest algorithm with the correct data.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8754/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 24, 2023, 4:11 AM UTC (344a898)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8754/a05b1ce...344a898/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 24, 2023, 4:11 AM UTC (344a898)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8754/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 24, 2023, 4:11 AM UTC (344a898)\">/links.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8754/a05b1ce...344a898/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 24, 2023, 4:11 AM UTC (344a898)\">diff</a> )",
